  (label "BTN1" (at 243.84 167.64 180) (fields_autoplaced) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid 7fc03099-b5ed-5f38-9129-7c46257ec5b2))
  (label "BTN2" (at 243.84 177.8 180) (fields_autoplaced) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid ec66a193-5f95-57d6-8e7b-fd63dcd0c390))
  (label "BTN3" (at 243.84 187.96 180) (fields_autoplaced) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid 1aafb1e7-aed1-59a7-9661-31f152294715))
  (text "Power input and breaker switch" (at 21.59 19.05 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid 05ee7470-f56f-5bea-b238-49ec9d5db7f7))
  (text "J1: female XT60 on the case, for the battery\n(LiFePO4 12.8 V 6 Ah with BMS) or a lab supply\n(12-14 V, current limit about 2 A).\nThe battery is charged off the mount.\nCB1: resettable breaker switch, 3-5 A, rated for DC." (at 22.86 46.99 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid c354ff59-7f5a-5933-8026-28aeb0b53636))
  (text "5 V supply for the ESP32 board" (at 21.59 67.31 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid 472ba45a-c790-5cd0-bc17-c31ed7596828))
  (text "U1 on a small TO-220 heatsink (tab = GND), about 1 W,\nnear C6/C7, which serve as its input capacitors.\nCB1 on: keep the ESP32 board's USB unplugged.\nUSB plugged in: keep CB1 off. The board's USB and\n5V pin are not meant to supply power together." (at 22.86 92.71 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 1cc84664-854f-5d8b-b3cd-ae7048bc40e9))
  (text "LEDs and buzzer (on the case)" (at 21.59 107.95 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid 5f2c1d19-f80e-5130-b3b2-d72a653c1e01))
  (text "GPIO high = LED or buzzer on. PWM sets the LED\nbrightness, or the tone of a passive buzzer." (at 22.86 138.43 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid effe07ff-7586-585e-bc7b-4bf17aa34092))
  (text "Controller" (at 125.73 19.05 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid 789bd338-a509-520d-98ae-3eb72ac50a4d))
  (text "Left free: GPIO0, 3, 45, 46 (strapping pins),\nGPIO19/20 (USB), GPIO35-37 (PSRAM on some boards),\nGPIO43/44 (USB serial console)." (at 165.1 116.84 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid c2093505-1ecd-5274-a6ed-bd48287e3f6c))
  (text "Stepper drivers" (at 242.57 19.05 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid fa21e5c2-57f9-57f4-b6c3-784112d6ac53))
  (text "Standalone mode, no UART: MS1 = GND, MS2 = 3V3 gives 1/64 microsteps.\nMotor current: potentiometer (Vref) on each module.\nC6, C7 must sit close to the VM pins: they absorb the motor voltage spikes." (at 246.38 106.68 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 9fe2e0b7-5a5a-550b-b6d4-f1ad68797fdb))
  (text "E-stop (on the case)" (at 21.59 153.67 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid 0ffb4832-4928-56c1-97dd-e663f0df23e7))
  (text "GPIO10 drives EN_OUT low to enable the drivers.\nE-stop pressed or ESP32 in reset: R3 pulls\nDRV_EN high and both drivers switch off.\nGPIO9 reads DRV_EN to detect it." (at 25.4 180.34 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 5255f410-f1de-53a2-af23-5f95a4dd4d84))
  (text "Hand-unit socket (case)" (at 100.33 153.67 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid deb88d27-d371-5cdf-9d1c-126c0ddad017))
  (text "Hand unit (on the cable)" (at 168.91 153.67 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid e615c65e-6d33-5a1f-8102-2239a3cd64b6))
  (text "Analog joystick module\n(GND, VCC, VRx, VRy, SW),\npowered from 3.3 V." (at 182.88 186.69 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 077c386d-b08c-5b68-884e-73baedbdb471))
  (text "Buttons and the joystick\nswitch use the ESP32\ninternal pull-ups." (at 269.24 165.1 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid cfd2eff2-b48e-5c22-88b0-b3a30b0fdd93))
  (text "Notes" (at 300.99 153.67 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid 98e8f8d6-c370-5484-8d23-cd090e511da5))
  (text "1. Supply, controller and drivers are all on the L:\n    no cable crosses the azimuth joint.\n2. +12V: 12.0-14.6 V from the battery or a lab supply.\n    It feeds the drivers and U1.\n3. TMC2209 header pin order differs between makers:\n    wire by pin name. VIO at 3.3 V (ESP32 logic level).\n4. Motor connectors: pins 1-2 one coil, 3-4 the other.\n5. A1 pins: 1-22 = header J1, 23-44 = header J3.\n6. Hand unit on an 8-wire cable (J2: for example\n    GX16-8, or RJ45 with a network cable).\n7. BZ1 directly on GPIO21: piezo buzzer, or active\n    buzzer drawing at most 20 mA at 3.3 V.\n8. Keep the blue LED dim at night." (at 302.26 158.75 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid f739246a-9d2e-56ae-9d05-7f00cdbd32b1))
